description:
 This is a combined synopsis/solicitation for commercial services prepared in accordance with the format in FAR subpart 12.6 and part 13, as supplemented with additional information included in this notice.&nbsp; This announcement constitutes the only solicitation; quotations are being requested and a written solicitation will not be issued.&nbsp; Solicitation number 34359RFQ270000002 is issued as a Request for Quotation (RFQ).&nbsp; This solicitation document and incorporated provisions and clauses are those in effect through Federal Acquisition Circular 2021-05, effective 10 March 2021. 

 The applicable North American Industry Classification Standard NAICS Code is 541990.&nbsp; This solicitation is 100% Set-Aside for Small Business. All responsible sources may submit a quotation which shall be considered by the agency.&nbsp; 

 It is anticipated that a firm-fixed price purchase order will be awarded for the item found below&nbsp;as a result of this synopsis/solicitation: 

 Equivalent&nbsp;items requested in this solicitation will be considered for award.. 

 SPECIFICATIONS: 

 The United States Coast Guard (USCG) National Strike Force (NSF) requires contractor support (training materials, equipment, and services) for instruction of Confined Space and Rescue Training&nbsp;for personnel in personal protective equipment for Level A and B responses in accordance with the attached Statement of Work. The final day will be dedicated to a skills exercise to evaluate how well participants apply the knowledge gained during the week&#39;s training. The contract will have a one-year period of performance. The Contractor will provide three (3) course convenings of up to twenty (20) students for Confined Space Entry Training and up to 12 students (that had the Confined Space Entry Course) for Confined Space Rescue Training. Both courses and exercise should be completed within 5 days (example: 2 days Entry, 2 days Rescue and 1 day skill exercise or something similar) and be completed prior to the last day of September 2027. The USCG will own the training courses, and a copy of all training materials created for the course shall be provided to the NSF. An audit will be completed to update material as needed due to regulation changes, mission changes and all other unforeseen circumstances. All training classes shall take place at USCG facilities.&nbsp; 

 The primary place of performance will be at the three National Strike Force Strike Teams (NSFSTs). The Government will provide all classroom facilities. There will be one convening per location. The locations of the three NSFSTs are:&nbsp; 



	 Atlantic Strike Team: Fort Dix, New Jersey&nbsp; 





	 Gulf Strike Team: Mobile, Alabama&nbsp; 





	 Pacific Strike Team: Novato, California 



